{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And Yitzhak trembled.</b> Rashi's explanation: he saw Gehenna opened beneath him, because he intended to curse Jacob. And one may say, Yitzhak said: if I erred between Esav and Jacob in this matter, I do not tremble and I have no wonder at it, for my eyes have grown dim and I did not recognize him. But at this I tremble — that nothing is hidden from the eyes of HaShem; how did He agree to transfer the birthright from the elder and give it to the younger? <b>[And he ate]</b> — the rule of the holy tongue: when the vowel is on the letter after the vav, they open it (i.e., it is read with a widened/passive form)." "<b>Moreover, he shall be blessed.</b> According to the spoken word I blessed him, for he acquired the birthright from you, and I did what is right. Another interpretation: <b>moreover, he shall be blessed</b> — for I already said to him, 'Those who curse you are cursed,' and if I curse him I curse myself, and therefore I do not wish to curse him. And if you ask: I will neither curse him nor bless him — I already said to him, 'Those who bless you are blessed,' therefore I bless him, for I am one who blesses you. Another interpretation: 'Moreover, he shall be blessed' — from the mouth of HaShem he is destined to be blessed."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:22.230307143Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}